+
+[[criterion]]
+id = "staff_mutation_success_receipts"
+name = "staff_mutation_success_receipts"
+type = "binary"
+weight = 2.0
+description = """
+Setup: After the core workflow, use Ruth and an ordinary roster with Leila active and Owen paused. Use a separate single-choice Receipt rehearsal ballot with Yes and No. Capture every staff mutation before its UI action and save the complete exchange immediately.
+Graded observations:
+1. Create Receipt rehearsal through the UI. Retain its successful create exchange, replay that exact request, and require the same status/body and exactly one draft and one create audit event. Edit the title to Receipt rehearsal approved through the UI and retain that success. Open it through the UI, retaining the Open success; its fixed snapshot must contain Leila only.
+2. Activate Owen, close Receipt rehearsal approved, pause Owen again, and publish that ballot, using visible controls and retaining each of these successful exchanges separately. Current ballot status must be Published with its original Leila-only snapshot and Owen currently paused. Each normal accepted action advances its applicable record revision once and contributes one relevant audit event.
+3. Replay all seven original successes: create, edit, Open, activation, Close, pause, Publish. Keep the original paths, bodies, operation identifiers and revisions as Ruth. Each must return its own original status/body rather than current-state output or a stale/terminal refusal. After each replay require unchanged current record identities, title, choices, Published status, revisions, Leila-only eligibility, paused roster, turnout/results and audit. In particular, the original activation response may say active, but it must not activate Owen again; Open must neither reopen the ballot nor capture a new snapshot; create must not duplicate it.
+4. Reuse the original create operation with the otherwise valid title Receipt collision. Require an explicit non-2xx mismatch refusal, no extra draft or audit, and the original create receipt still replaying identically. This group tests staff successes once, not seven separately weighted siblings.
+5. After each of the two existing trusted restarts, repeat all seven exact-success replays and the current-state comparisons, using the retained originals. Do not inspect SQLite or manufacture an operation field absent from the app. A missing required staff operation mechanism is not a pass.
+"""
+
+[[criterion]]
+id = "roster_conflict_snapshot_chain"
+name = "roster_conflict_snapshot_chain"
+type = "binary"
+weight = 2.0
+description = """
+Setup: Use two ordinary Ruth tabs in the same browser context and distinct UI-created single-choice ballots named Roster includes Owen and Roster excludes Owen, each with Yes and No. Keep Leila active. Establish Owen active through a normal UI action if needed, then have both tabs read the same actual membership revision R and active state.
+Graded observations:
+1. In tab A pause Owen and then activate him again, waiting for each accepted action and capturing each genuine request shape. Require two accepted revision advances and one audit event per action. His value is active again, but its revision is now newer than R.
+2. Attempt tab B's stale Pause with revision R and a fresh operation identifier. Prefer its ordinary stale UI control. If the app automatically refreshed tab B, adapt only the actual captured membership request to R and active=false; do not mutate browser state or count a newly current request as stale. Require non-2xx stale refusal with useful refresh guidance. Reread the roster and audit: Owen remains active at the newer revision and no refusal audit event was added.
+3. Through the UI create/open Roster includes Owen. Its snapshot must include exactly Leila and Owen, and it must be visible to Owen after refresh. A stale refusal alone is insufficient: the accepted roster must reach this downstream eligibility result.
+4. Refresh tab B, make its now-current Pause succeed, and create/open Roster excludes Owen. Require a Leila-only snapshot, absent for Owen but visible to Leila. Roster includes Owen must still contain both Members and remain visible to Owen. Do not require a particular revision field name or per-member versus whole-roster implementation; compare the applicable version actually used by the app.
+5. After each of the same two existing restarts, require Owen still paused, the two ballots still Open, their exact respective snapshots and role-appropriate visibility unchanged, and no return of the stale write or extra membership audit. Own these conflict-driven snapshots here, not under the earlier ordinary fixed-snapshot criterion.
+"""
+
+[[criterion]]
+id = "refusal_receipt_after_state_change"
+name = "refusal_receipt_after_state_change"
+type = "binary"
+weight = 2.0
+description = """
+Setup: Use Ruth and a separate UI-created single-choice Refusal rehearsal ballot with Yes and No. Discover the real edit and Publish shapes from successful UI interactions. Use well-formed authorized requests; malformed fields, unknown records or wrong roles cannot substitute for the required recorded domain refusals.
+Graded observations:
+1. Create the draft, then visibly edit its context to Board review A. Using the observed edit shape, submit Board review B with the earlier draft revision and a fresh operation identifier. Require a stale refusal and unchanged accepted context, revision and audit; retain its exact request/status/body. Now visibly save Board review C using current data. Replay the original stale request unchanged: it must return its original refusal details and status, not a newly computed refusal based on the later revision, and must not restore Board review A or B. A fresh legitimate edit is the positive control.
+2. Open Refusal rehearsal through the UI. Adapt the genuine Publish shape to this ballot at its current Open revision with a fresh operation identifier. Require a non-2xx wrong-state refusal and unchanged Open ballot/audit; retain that exchange independently. Close the ballot normally. Replay the same refused Publish with its original operation identifier and revision: require the identical stored refusal and unchanged Closed state, not an automatic publication or a different newly calculated stale response.
+3. A fresh current-revision Publish operation through the UI must now succeed. Replay both original refused operations again while Published. Require their original statuses and bodies, unchanged final Board review C context, Published status, revisions, eligibility, turnout/results and audit. Reuse of a failed operation is not a new attempt.
+4. After each of the two existing trusted restarts, repeat both refused-operation replays and the exact current-state comparisons. Receipt storage may change privately at the original refusal; it must never create a public audit event or change an accepted record. Do not require preservation of unauthorized or malformed requests.
+"""
